hqc — provenance note
======================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling
`bip340`/`xmss`/`bls12_381` modules — self-contained crypto modules
not folded into the root NOTICE).

Provenance
----------

hqc — clean-room implementation from the official HQC specification
("Hamming Quasi-Cyclic (HQC)", 22/08/2025, pqc-hqc.org — the spec
accompanying NIST's March-2025 selection of HQC as a code-based KEM
backup to ML-KEM). A public specification, not a copyrightable work; no
third-party source was ported.

Design reference (behavior/byte-layout only, no source copied): the
reference implementation, https://gitlab.com/pqc-hqc/hqc, tag `v5.0.0`
(public-domain license — see that repo's own LICENSE), consulted for
exact algorithmic behavior the spec's prose leaves underspecified:

- The `Xof.getBytes` 8-byte stream-consumption rounding quirk
  (`prng.zig`) — reference: `xof_get_bytes` in `src/common/symmetric.c`.
- The Barrett-reduction / 24-bit-rejection-threshold / duplicate-scan
  constant-access-pattern shapes of both fixed-weight samplers
  (`prng.zig`'s `sampleFixedWeightRejection`/`sampleFixedWeightBiased`)
  — reference: `src/ref/vector.c`'s
  `vect_generate_random_support{1,2}`/`vect_write_support_to_vector`.

Test-vector oracle (also design-reference, not ported source): the same
tag's `kats/ref/hqc-1/intermediates_values` file — a byte-exact,
independently-verified fixture embedded in `src/kat_vectors.zig` (fetched
via `curl` directly from gitlab.com and cross-checked in Python's
`hashlib` before transcription, specifically to avoid hex-transcription
risk from any summarizing intermediary). See SPEC.md's Verification
section for exactly which primitives are numeric-KAT-pinned against this
fixture vs. transcribed-from-source-only.

No other third-party source was ported or consulted. Uses only the Zig
standard library (`std.crypto.hash.sha3`: SHAKE256, SHA3-256, SHA3-512).

This is Part 1 of a multi-part arc (ring + PRNG foundation only — see
SPEC.md's "Arc plan"); Parts 2 (Reed-Muller/Reed-Solomon decoder) and 3
(PKE/KEM composition, byte-exact KAT) will consult the same reference tag
and should extend this file rather than duplicate its header.
